Field requirements:
- title: a standardized, professional vulnerability name (10-26 characters, e.g. "external account authentication bypass leading to admin takeover"). If the raw name is already well-formed (e.g. includes a CVE), keep or lightly adjust it — do not copy the summary.
- target: the affected host or URL, extracted from the summary/evidence; an empty string if undeterminable.
- description: 1 paragraph, 2-3 sentences. State exactly three things — what the vulnerability is, where it occurs, and the root cause. Do not stack OWASP categories, restate fixes, or pad.
- module: the owning functional module (short, e.g. "external account login / unauthenticated endpoint").
- risk_analysis: 2-4 items, one sentence each, each a concrete consequence of THIS vulnerability on THIS target (who can do what, what data or privileges they gain). If there is no concrete consequence, write fewer — never filler like "may affect system security".
- remediation: 2-4 items, one sentence each, specific and actionable (which point to change, how, what to verify). Never vague items like "raise security awareness" or "conduct regular audits".
- CVSS 3.1: cvss_score (number), cvss_vector (e.g. "AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"), cvss_metrics (the eight English values, e.g. {"AV":"Network","AC":"Low","PR":"None","UI":"None","S":"Unchanged","C":"High","I":"High","A":"High"}).

Do not output test_process — the platform generates reproduction steps directly from real evidence; return "test_process":[].

Output JSON only: {"title":"...","target":"...","description":["..."],"module":"...","test_process":[],"risk_analysis":["..."],"remediation":["..."],"cvss_score":0,"cvss_vector":"...","cvss_metrics":{...}}

